---
/**
 * What this site records, and how to stop it.
 *
 * The card and its switch are the handoff's §11. The three things listed are
 * this site's, not the prototype's: the layout choice goes to a first-party
 * endpoint, and saying so is the point — an ad blocker will not catch it, so
 * the switch here is the only thing that will.
 *
 * Written before the endpoints it describes exist. The flag works from the day
 * the switch does, and whatever loads them reads it.
 */
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What emptystat.es records, and how to opt out."
>
  <div class="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>What this site records</h1>

    <p>
      Page views, through Plausible: cookieless, aggregate, and nothing set on
      your device. It records that a page was viewed, not who viewed it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Which gallery layout you pick. That choice goes to an endpoint on this
      domain, so it is first-party and <strong
        >an ad blocker will not stop it</strong
      > — the switch below will. What arrives is a count per layout with nothing
      attached to it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Search queries, stored so the gallery can be improved against what people
      look for. The text, and no identifier beside it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Submissions store the image, the metadata typed with it, and the credit
      chosen. No email address is asked for, and a submitted image can be
      removed on request.
    </p>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-row">
        <div>
          <p class="card-title">Opt out of analytics</p>
          <p class="card-state" id="optout-state">
            On. Aggregate page views only, no cookies or identifiers.
          </p>
        </div>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="optout"
          class="switch-control"
          role="switch"
          aria-checked="false"
          aria-label="Opt out of analytics"></button>
      </div>

      <p class="card-note" id="optout-note" hidden>
        Your browser is sending a Do Not Track signal, which this site honours
        before anything else. No analytics run on your visit, and this switch is
        locked because there is nothing left for it to turn off. If you turn Do
        Not Track off in your browser settings, the switch here becomes yours to
        set.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="footnote dotted">
      <span>Last changed 17 August 2026</span>
      <span>removal requests: remove@emptystat.es</span>
    </p>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var KEY = "es:optout";
      var button = document.getElementById("optout");
      var state = document.getElementById("optout-state");
      var note = document.getElementById("optout-note");

      // A browser signal counts as opting out and is not reversible from here:
      // the reader already answered this one level up.
      var signalled =
        navigator.doNotTrack === "1" ||
        navigator.globalPrivacyControl === true;

      function render() {
        var out = signalled || localStorage.getItem(KEY) === "1";
        button.setAttribute("aria-checked", String(out));
        button.disabled = signalled;
        note.hidden = !signalled;
        state.textContent = signalled
          ? "Off. Nothing is being recorded for this visit."
          : out
            ? "Off. Nothing is recorded for this browser. The choice is stored locally, not on a server."
            : "On. Aggregate page views only, no cookies or identifiers.";
      }

      button.addEventListener("click", function () {
        if (signalled) return;
        if (localStorage.getItem(KEY) === "1") localStorage.removeItem(KEY);
        else localStorage.setItem(KEY, "1");
        render();
      });

      try {
        render();
      } catch (e) {}
    })();
  </script>
</Layout>
